  "footnote": "Major courses require C- or better; S is acceptable when a course offers S/U, except performance courses used as electives must be letter-graded. Declaration requires three Music courses totaling at least 5 credits with a B-minus average, contacting the Director of Undergraduate Studies, meeting a faculty advisor, and an application. MUSIC 1100 or MUSIC 1199 may qualify for declaration but neither counts toward the major. Choose electives with your advisor; exploring at least two musical traditions is strongly encouraged. Specializations are optional course sequences, not required tracks. Optional senior honors involves an independent thesis, music-making project, or both; the new honors criteria apply to 2026-27 graduates. FWS courses and ENGL 2860/2880 used for FWS cannot count toward the major.",
